  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22886375
    description: "version 0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
abstract: >
  flybench scores a connectome-constrained neural model (the reference is a uniform leaky
  integrate-and-fire on the FlyWire v783 and MaleCNS v1.0 connectomes) against published fly
  behaviour: 37 tasks (the task set frozen at v1.0), each a stimulus, a readout and thresholds
  with a DOI-cited source or a stated convention, every one pre-registered as an RFC with
  predictions before its first run, scored with graded margins, ceiling and floor gates, seeds,
  and shuffled-wiring controls. Three pinned builds of FlyWire v783 (Codex, Codex with blank
  transmitters signed, and Shiu et al. 2024's published graph) are scored side by side.
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - MaleCNS
  - benchmark
  - leaky integrate-and-fire
